# Application layer

Contains all business logic. Organized per feature:
`application/<feature>/{use-cases,ports,read-models}/`.

- **Use cases** are classes named `<Verb><Entity>UseCase` (e.g.
  `CreateApplicationUseCase`) with a single `execute(input)` method. One class
  per operation — see `mutate-application.use-cases.ts` for the pattern of
  co-locating Create/Update/Delete use cases for one entity.
- **Ports** are interfaces only (e.g. `job-applications.repository.ts`) —
  no implementation, no Prisma types.
- **Read models** (`read-models/*.record.ts`) describe the shape returned to
  Presentation — plain types, not Prisma types.
- Must never import `@prisma/client`, `hono`, or any concrete repository class.
- Errors: throw typed errors from `application/shared/errors/app-error.ts`
  (e.g. `NotFoundError`), never raw `Error`. Use `assert-resource.ts` helpers
  for ownership/existence checks.
- Validate ownership (`userId`) inside the use case, not just in the route.
